      "summary": "The interface wiring, model mappings, test coverage, CI job, and migration identity boundary match the issue. The migration can fail on a freshly provisioned Azure SQL database because it does not create the audit schema.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api/Persistence/Migrations/20261014190000_InitialCaseStateSchema.cs",
          "line": 56,
          "message": "Create the audit schema before creating audit.case_events; the SQLite migration test does not expose this because SQLite ignores schemas.",
          "confidence": 0.94,
          "category": "logic-error",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "The migration creates audit.case_events, but its Up method does not create the audit schema. The repository's Terraform grants reference that schema but do not create it.",
            "failureScenario": "On a fresh Azure SQL database provisioned by this repository, applying the migration reaches CREATE TABLE [audit].[case_events] before the audit schema exists, so SQL Server rejects the migration."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "agentId": "test-reviewer-codex",
