        "minor": 0,
        "suggestion": 0
      },
      "summary": "The interface and EF model are covered by the named tests, and the referenced Terraform grants separate app data access from migration authority. AC2's SQLite test cannot catch a migration that places a table in the wrong schema.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api.Tests/SqlCaseStateStoreTests.cs",
          "line": 49,
          "message": "AC2 does not verify that the migration itself creates case_events in the audit schema; the SQLite migration test ignores schemas and validates only the EF model mapping.",
          "confidence": 0.93,
          "category": "testing",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "AC2 applies the migration with SQLite, then checks the EF model schema with AssertMapped and checks only table names in sqlite_master. SQLite ignores schema names when applying migrations.",
            "failureScenario": "If the migration creates case_events in dbo instead of audit, this test still passes: SQLite creates the case_events table, while AssertMapped checks the model's audit mapping rather than the migration's schema. The migration would therefore violate the required Azure SQL schema without CI catching it."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
